    example: "A 12 V supply feeds node A through R1 = 1 kΩ, and two resistors R2 = R3 = 2 kΩ run from node A to ground. Unknown: V_A. KCL at A says the current arriving through R1 equals the currents leaving through R2 and R3: (12 − V_A)/1 kΩ = V_A/2 kΩ + V_A/2 kΩ. The right side simplifies to V_A/1 kΩ, so 12 − V_A = V_A and V_A = 6 V. Currents: 6 mA flows in through R1, splitting into 3 mA and 3 mA. Check KVL: 6 V across R1 plus 6 V across R2 equals the 12 V supply. The app's simulator does exactly this, just with dozens of nodes at once.",
